---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - SwasthaTrack"
  description="SwasthaTrack privacy policy detailing patient healthcare data privacy, ABDM compliance, and cryptographic security."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-8 sm:p-12 shadow-sm space-y-8">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400">Legal & Data Governance</span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-1">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2">Effective Date: August 1, 2026 • Version 2.0 (ABDM Compliant)</p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. ABDM & Health Data Privacy Framework</h2>
          <p>
            SwasthaTrack is engineered in strict compliance with the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM) and national health data confidentiality standards. All personal health records (PHR), electronic medical records (EMR), and diagnostic pathology findings are strictly protected under consent-based encryption protocols.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Information Collection & Usage</h2>
          <p>
            When registering patients into our clinical triage engine, we collect:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            <li>Demographic identifiers (Full Name, Contact Number, Age, Gender, Blood Group).</li>
            <li>Clinical vitals (Blood pressure, body temperature, pulse oximetry readings).</li>
            <li>Chief symptom complaints used strictly by the AI triage engine for urgency classification.</li>
            <li>Prescription and laboratory diagnostic records generated by licensed medical professionals.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Artificial Intelligence & Clinical Data Safety</h2>
          <p>
            Patient symptoms processed by SwasthaTrack's AI triage engine are sanitized and utilized solely for immediate real-time queue classification and consultation assistance. No patient clinical data is ever sold or utilized for third-party commercial advertising.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. Data Retention & Cryptographic Security</h2>
          <p>
            All persistent medical data is stored within secure, access-controlled databases utilizing AES-256 encryption at rest and TLS 1.3 encryption in transit. Role-based access control (RBAC) ensures only authorized physicians, pharmacists, and pathologists access pertinent clinical records.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. Contact Our Data Protection Officer</h2>
          <p>
            For privacy inquiries or consent revocation requests, reach our compliance team at <a href="mailto:privacy@swasthatrack.org" class="text-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-400 font-semibold underline">privacy@swasthatrack.org</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
